exactly `k` hidden layers, i.e. `f = T^(k+1) ∘ ReLU ∘ T^(k) ∘ ⋯ ∘ ReLU ∘ T^(1)`
for some affine transformations `T^(1), …, T^(k+1)` of matching dimensions. -/
def ComputesReLU : (n k : ℕ) → ((Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ) → Prop
  | n, 0, f => ∃ T : AffineMapRn n 1, ∀ x, f x = T.eval x 0
  | n, (k + 1), f =>
