/-! ## `depth` : PROVED

Both bounds are `⌈log₃(n-1)⌉ + 1`; Mathlib's `Real.natCeil_logb_natCast` says exactly
`⌈Real.logb b n⌉₊ = Nat.clog b n` for natural `b n` (no extra side conditions), so once
we rewrite `(n:ℝ) - 1` as `((n - 1 : ℕ) : ℝ)` (using `n ≥ 3 ≥ 1`) the two bounds match. -/
theorem depth (n : ℕ) (hn : 3 ≤ n) :
